# Urban Heat — environment template. Copy to `.env` and fill in.
# `.env` is gitignored; this template is committed.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Supabase (OPTIONAL for Sprint 1)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Sprint 1 is local-only: SQLite recording works fully without these. When they
# are absent the app runs in "local-only mode" and cloud sign-in is disabled.
#
# The EXPO_PUBLIC_ prefix is required for the value to be inlined into the app
# bundle. The anon key is a public client key by design — but it is still
# project-identifying, so it stays out of source control.
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Google Maps (Android)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# react-native-maps uses the Google provider on Android and renders a BLANK GREY
# map without a key. An absent key is not a build failure — it degrades
# gracefully so database and BLE work is never blocked on cloud procurement.
#
# Needs "Maps SDK for Android" enabled on a Google Cloud project with billing.
# NOTE: read WITHOUT the EXPO_PUBLIC_ prefix, because it is consumed by
# app.config.ts at build time (not at runtime), and injected into the native
# manifest rather than the JS bundle.
GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY=
